# AICTE CaseSync — Full Application Upgrade and Backend Implementation Prompt

## 1. Main objective

Upgrade the existing AICTE CaseSync project into a fully functional, production-oriented web application for integrated institution complaint monitoring and cross-Bureau coordination.

Modify the existing codebase rather than creating an unrelated project. Inspect the current frontend, `WorkspaceApp.tsx`, routing, components, styles, state management, and available backend integrations before making changes.

Implement the following requirements:

1. Smooth sliding transitions whenever users click and switch between main navigation sections.
2. Apply the same transitions to nested pages, sub-items, tabs, detail views, and other navigable sections.
3. Remove the demo-mode experience, including demo-role labels, demo login selectors, and demo-specific navigation.
4. Implement real authentication and backend-enforced role-based access control.
5. Hide the top navigation bar when the user scrolls down and reveal it when scrolling up.
6. Create a dedicated `backend/` directory containing the server, APIs, database integration, authentication, business logic, and configuration.
7. Connect the existing frontend to the backend through actual API requests.
8. Preserve the current light theme as the default, dark theme support, neumorphic styling, and existing CaseSync visual identity.
9. Implement institution management, complaint tracking, cross-Bureau overlap detection, transfers, coordination, deadline alerts, reports, and audit history.
10. Test the entire application instead of stopping at visual implementation.

**Important:** Do not simply rename “Demo Mode” to “Live Mode.” Remove simulated authentication and frontend-only authorization, and implement genuine server-side authentication and permissions.

If external AICTE systems, official datasets, or production credentials are unavailable, build a functioning standalone application with persistent data and clearly documented integration requirements. Do not claim it is connected to real AICTE systems unless that integration exists.

