## 10. Implement backend alert generation

Create:

`backend/src/services/deadline-monitor.ts`

and

`backend/src/services/notification-service.ts`

Generate alerts for:

- Potential cross-Bureau overlaps.
- Uncertain institution identity.
- Approaching configured deadlines.
- Overdue cases.
- Coordination awaiting action.
- Transfers awaiting acceptance.
- Escalations awaiting review.

Use configurable deadline thresholds. Do not assume official statutory deadlines without a verified source or explicit configuration.

Use a scheduled worker or another suitable server-side mechanism to recalculate time-based alerts.

Make alert generation idempotent so repeated runs do not create duplicate alerts.

A case status change, transfer acceptance, relationship review, or coordination resolution should update the appropriate alerts.

Keep read status separate from issue resolution.

Use database-backed notifications. If real-time delivery is implemented, use the project's established WebSocket, Server-Sent Events, or notification mechanism. Otherwise, use reliable API refresh behavior and do not claim instant cross-user updates.

